Nope. None of the obvious ideas work. Water-gushing obliterates
engravings, as does melting ice. You can't engrave while
water-walking, or even while magically breathing. However...

If I read the source right, teleportation checks whether the subject
(when a monster) is water-breathing, and if it's not a
water-non-breaathing monster, it considers water squares
"valid". Thus, engraving over an extant burned engraving with a wand
of teleportation has a small chance of relocating the engraving to a
water square. AFAICT, that's the only situation where an engraving can
be on water.

